From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: soc-utils: do not log -ENXIO in snd_soc_ret()

The SDG voice boards place a wlf,wm8960 node on a bus with no WM8960.
Every codec register access then fails with -ENXIO, because i2c-mt65xx
returns that error on an unacknowledged transfer. snd_soc_ret() prints
an "ASoC error" line for every errno outside its allow list, so card
bring-up fills the log.

Add -ENXIO to the allow list. The function only suppresses the message
and returns the same value, so no caller changes behaviour. These
boards use only the PCM path of the codec, not the control path.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 sound/soc/soc-utils.c |    7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/soc/soc-utils.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-utils.c
@@ -29,6 +29,13 @@ int snd_soc_ret(const struct device *dev
 	case -EPROBE_DEFER:
 	case -ENOTSUPP:
 	case -EOPNOTSUPP:
+	/*
+	 * i2c-mt65xx returns -ENXIO when a transfer gets no
+	 * acknowledgement. A board that names a codec it does not
+	 * carry then logs one ASoC error for every access. Suppress
+	 * the message only; snd_soc_ret() returns the error as before.
+	 */
+	case -ENXIO:
 		break;
 	default:
 		va_start(args, fmt);
